Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Part II. The pairing, the three methods, the ground states and the gauge \
bosons in the superfluid\
\>", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"97f1830b-696d-41bd-9b01-fb6486713011"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part II treats item 6 of the problem (Sections 8 to 11 of the manuscript): \
which interaction binds two spinor charges into a pair of spin zero and which \
gauge boson mediates the pairing; the methods of Hubbard and Stratonovich \
(HS), Kohn and Sham (KS) and Cornwall, Jackiw and Tomboulis (CJT); the \
recursion of the potential until all three methods admit a superfluid; the \
ground states, the first excited states and the gap; and the gauge bosons in \
the superfluid. The checks of this part are those of the Python program ",
 StyleBox["sf_part2.py",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "; like that program, the notebook compares its own results with the values \
of the Rust program ",
 StyleBox["sf_part2",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", which the next (closed) cell holds: they were copied from the data files \
of the Rust program by ",
 StyleBox["wolfram/tools/make_data_cells.py",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", whose comment at the top of the cell names the files and their SHA-256 \
checksums. The notebook reads no file."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4bad4028-699e-43f5-af07-08451a5a2500"],

