Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Part III, first section. The Landau form of the effective potentials: what it \
is, how accurate it is, and why that matters\
\>", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"dcd4fc94-cedc-48ee-950a-15f39710c025"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part III of the solution builds the effective Lagrangians ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["CJT",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6af3bd5b-32be-4b4a-b209-202a3938f4ce"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["HS",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "409d9aec-d035-42c1-b625-2cf1e037521e"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["KS",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f98dfc3-2179-47ca-b982-7150fe25ad64"],
 " of the field of the superfluid boson singlet state. Their potential parts \
were summarized by a polynomial, the Landau form, with the remark: \"The \
Landau form is a fit; its largest residual is 0.27-0.7 % of the depth\". The \
author asked (21 November 2026) to explain this remark clearly and completely \
and why it is important, to define the Landau form with examples, and to keep \
the answer in the documents and in this notebook. This chapter is that \
answer. It is the first section of Part III in the notebook; the next chapter \
(Section III.T) is the second, and the other sections of Part III follow in \
the next versions. The computed curves are taken from the Rust program ",
 StyleBox["sf_part3",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " (the closed cell of Section III.L.3, with the SHA-256 checksums of its \
data files), and this chapter recomputes from them, by its own least squares, \
every number of the answer; the engine of Part II, which computes such \
states, is used by the next chapter."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f5114406-8adc-4bcf-9b10-002afa0f52c0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["III.L.1 The objects", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4060f9c4-a022-4afd-875b-e0bf319b2b6a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The field and its effective potential.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The field of the superfluid boson singlet state is the complex isospin \
vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "1"}]], ",", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "2"}]], ",", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "3"}]]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "798679f6-8df3-4298-a0ba-b47810ff9ab7"],
 " of the amplitudes of the pair self-energy of a uniform state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P",
      FontFamily->"Helvetica",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", "\[Iota]",
     LimitsPositioning->True], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "\[Iota]"}]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["K",
        FontFamily->"Helvetica",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["LL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Iota]"], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34cf65ac-8ac2-42c1-bb93-be993c99fb48"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K",
     FontFamily->"Helvetica",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Iota]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fde2d34f-3cb8-4046-b137-13543d9dcdec"],
 " are the three pair matrices of Part I (",
 StyleBox["kLL[iota]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " in the code) and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f62434d5-4253-44bf-bdac-5c84f09ac513"],
 " is one of the five computed methods: HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "995e497a-e694-4205-bdaa-4c697980d7d2"],
 ", HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cbd1f6e5-0ae8-454d-9501-93d280d7ab25"],
 ", HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f6d11b1f-d074-47b1-9daa-2df02b98eb11"],
 " (the method of Hubbard and Stratonovich with the shares ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["HS",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["S",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c957bda-7980-4296-aac2-d2992996dda4"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["HS",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["V",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "90397c15-c70b-434c-b180-92d98e7599b7"],
 " of the scalar and the vector term decoupled in the density channels), KS \
(Kohn and Sham) and CJT (Cornwall, Jackiw and Tomboulis). The effective \
potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], ")"}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "692c572c-b692-4311-b2e9-5aa5d3133763"],
 " is the smallest energy per volume of method ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01d986cf-dedc-4ff6-9d39-792ea15fe896"],
 " among the uniform states whose field is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c4aa858b-1aa0-4556-91af-70dae756d652"],
 ", measured from the normal vacuum, so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", "0", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a557e33-29c0-415c-843c-4f5afe8c35c2"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"af45e619-10e7-4d1a-9f8e-03025dcd559b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How it is computed.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A fixed pair self-energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["a",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["K",
        FontFamily->"Helvetica",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["LL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c4195ae-aa4a-4d8c-821c-370976a30b9b"],
 ", the applied field of amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["a",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34394de2-89d8-4b20-a846-4b29a0a7ee98"],
 ", is put into the matrix of Bogoliubov and de Gennes, the normal \
self-energy is made self-consistent, and the ground state gives one point: \
its own field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    "\[CapitalPhi]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "3"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62ca17c0-16e6-4d9e-8a15-6d299a0b10c6"],
 " and its energy per volume. The Rust program computes 61 points per method, \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["a",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "24c02e03-7fa5-43a0-bddf-dfce2f57c7b1"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8688a426-021d-4df9-ad0f-fb0f3da6ec04"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f170404b-8566-409f-972b-132f78c4522b"],
 ", each self-consistent to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "13"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cecb9c56-5a23-495b-ad70-dae9f7b536b7"],
 ". Along the ",
 StyleBox["polar",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " fields ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[CurlyTheta]"}]], "\[CapitalPhi]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "230ac318-bc69-437b-9255-484657441df9"],
 " (real phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[CurlyTheta]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0aebf3c6-0e8f-4d20-9987-2ea53d989c0c"],
 ", real unit vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8fd0fc16-5418-4d20-9e8d-3945aebdc416"],
 ") the potential depends on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalPhi]", "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56ff4479-b41f-4939-9091-aaaf17fa8e89"],
 " alone. Its minimum lies at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d97ca625-d4b5-4b8d-996d-2ed702b7d14f"],
 " (the vacuum), and the ",
 StyleBox["depth",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
       StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ")"}]}], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d97aa14-a243-4610-817d-05181ab540db"],
 " is the energy per volume by which the superfluid lies below the normal \
vacuum. The second derivative ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["amp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b0b5c2d5-50fd-4432-9932-087f53d811d9"],
 " of the polar curve at its minimum fixes the mass of the amplitude mode, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["amp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cca6a41-17e5-4bf8-a679-5e4147991606"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2938cc96-f2dc-4d31-881f-af03ebd83574"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "436a2d82-7171-4ff1-a0bb-4d451d3ad017"],
 " are the two coefficients of the kinetic part of the effective Lagrangian."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c19bf40b-67a8-47e5-86b5-85136da123d8"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["III.L.2 The Landau form: definition and examples", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b4b330d9-7d54-4a86-a3a9-0b947d496538"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A Landau form of a potential is its expansion in powers of the order \
parameter (the field that vanishes in the symmetric state and not in the \
broken one) under two rules: only polynomial invariants of the symmetry group \
occur, and the expansion stops after the lowest orders that bound the \
potential from below and produce its minima. L. D. Landau introduced it for \
phase transitions (1937): near a continuous transition the order parameter is \
small, the free energy is assumed to be analytic in it, and the form is its \
Taylor expansion, whose coefficients (the Landau coefficients) are \
derivatives at the symmetric state. The quadratic coefficient changes its \
sign at the transition; the signs of the higher coefficients decide the order \
of the transition and which broken state is the minimum. Examples:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"49ce49fd-ece7-4f4d-b99b-29a23fdd1348"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A uniaxial ferromagnet: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "adff802c-048d-469d-822f-cda93b0feebd"],
 " for the magnetization ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["mag",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1037e7f-90f4-4e94-a7ac-b2d36295ab96"],
 " (the symmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightArrow]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["mag",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "99d95d68-562a-41c0-acd4-7f808949974a"],
 "), with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["mag",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aa68896b-2e83-4603-9a97-caf328be6b3b"],
 " proportional to the temperature minus the Curie temperature and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01179345-8826-422f-b757-86594b9a9a92"],
 "; below the Curie temperature the minima are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["mag",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["mag",
            FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d0822469-9801-4904-9b65-9246a0093ff8"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d6ae4975-0c88-47e6-96bf-2950e0cd0be3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The theory of superconductivity of V. L. Ginzburg and L. D. Landau (1950): ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
       StyleBox["GL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
       StyleBox["GL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "24415d8f-3930-4120-aa69-ae02aafa25d7"],
 " for the complex pair wave function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
    StyleBox["GL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5cd52163-48b0-4000-b296-522858e4cb8b"],
 " (the symmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9db2aca0-b1ab-40cf-b814-5c53912efe8b"],
 "), with gradient terms and the magnetic field added. L. P. Gor'kov (1959) \
derived it from the theory of Bardeen, Cooper and Schrieffer near the \
critical temperature, where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a31425b1-2daa-4471-acc9-d6fecd733229"],
 " is small; there the coefficients are true Taylor coefficients."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"378c4942-1b41-42af-9187-418910f5a3a9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Higgs potential of the Standard Model, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Mu]", 
        StyleBox["SM",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "2"]}], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SM",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
         SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
          StyleBox["SM",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
       SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
        StyleBox["SM",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9d3a5079-9ab1-437b-b23c-813fb4754543"],
 ": the doublet ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["SM",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cb9c8bf-882d-4082-9994-8fa045ee8a49"],
 " has the single invariant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SM",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "617a89d2-1192-490f-9dcd-344b4a5bbf8f"],
 " of degree 2, and this Landau form is exact at tree level, not a truncation."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bf2f04b0-bf0a-4020-b06f-2d842cce2f3c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Bose-Einstein condensates of spin 1 (T.-L. Ho, 1998; T. Ohmi and K. \
Machida, 1998), the closest analogue of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31dcece0-d437-4ba6-ac90-7d0fac59d827"],
 ": their order parameter is a complex vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "744a7df7-f316-4a51-b0b7-0cc5c85c27ac"],
 ", and their energy per volume ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["n",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
        OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
        "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
         OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
        "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "df471572-709b-4d5e-81bb-bb505440581e"],
 " contains the same two quartic invariants as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5fb9c7d4-97f7-4a0d-b7ed-02402c4a43f4"],
 ", the second term being the square of the spin. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1bb96ff5-5096-42c7-9a14-2d34040210ac"],
 " (sodium-23) favors the polar state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "<", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "142a5a3a-6dc9-48c9-af65-3748483ab9e1"],
 " (rubidium-87) the ferromagnetic state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Proportional]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], ",", "0"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8421202a-0852-4249-a985-cadff23038cc"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"eaaafe54-1465-4ccf-9f03-9271e13d7026"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ferroelectric barium titanate (A. F. Devonshire, 1949): ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "6"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "efaa6434-76a5-4e37-bbd1-bc9119bf4bc1"],
 " for the polarization ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["D",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e9816214-773d-47b0-94f6-6850ecd51f2f"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "<", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d6c7a9f-8b40-4a04-a992-b706c0ab0a9f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d9f62d0d-f9fc-4a8e-88ee-692e57747520"],
 ": the sixth power is required, and the transition is of first order."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"24d1792f-dacb-4710-8b15-16780b13e6fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Superfluid helium-3 (A. J. Leggett, 1975): one quadratic and five quartic \
invariants of a complex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b5d214-288a-4141-a42b-6dd5dae357b4"],
 " matrix, whose five coefficients decide between the phases A and B. The \
nematic liquid crystals (P. G. de Gennes, 1971): the traceless symmetric \
tensor of the nematic order admits an invariant of the third degree, so the \
transition is of first order."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d4c50a78-19da-4b08-8b61-254dcbda2ffb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The name has nothing to do with the Landau levels of a charge in a magnetic \
field (Section I.6 of this notebook, AS2): the same physicist, another \
subject. ",
 StyleBox["The Landau form of $\\vec\\Phi$.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The symmetry is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "000fce9f-029f-4081-9967-c062920e4b0c"],
 ". The independent invariants up to the fourth degree are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b4b2a9b-e4cf-44cb-ae2f-85dffc8df985"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b336875-dd02-4a3f-943b-f4c369a764c8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78dbae48-9293-413f-b970-ce7385627d42"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Times]", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "*"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c4bfd211-8063-4428-b983-494476b107d7"],
 " vanishes exactly on the polar fields. The Landau form used by the solution \
is"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5c9bdc01-3dea-4fde-9692-21927456909a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
