Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["III.T.2 The values of the Rust program", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4698f1ed-5a55-4694-92b7-cd3cc307fe2e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The closed cell holds the thermal results of the Rust program ",
 StyleBox["sf_part3",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ": ",
 StyleBox["rustThermal",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " (per method and reduced temperature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["c",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23a23814-b40b-4c1e-964d-7676b5aa9a55"],
 ": the temperature, the order parameter, the Dirac masses of the superfluid \
and of the normal state, the gap, the radius of convergence, the free energy \
at the minimum, the difference of the entropies, the residual of the gap \
equation, the Taylor coefficients, the order parameter of Landau's theory and \
the number of iterations), ",
 StyleBox["rustThermalLandau",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " (the residuals of the Landau forms) and ",
 StyleBox["rustThermalCurves",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " (the free-energy curves: the applied field, the field of the state and its \
free energy). They were copied from the data files named, with their SHA-256 \
checksums, in the comment at the top of the cell, by ",
 StyleBox["wolfram/tools/make_data_cells.py",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f342486a-e7a6-4af3-9df3-0e5a4dbf4171"],

