Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How wide is the critical region?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The Ginzburg number is 7.6 to 11.4, far above 1. The condition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["red",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "\[GreaterGreater]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Gi",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d5adbe68-4c9f-45a4-b9a0-e73b2ba2ac4b"],
 " of mean-field theory therefore holds at no temperature where the form of \
Ginzburg and Landau applies: even at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["red",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}],
    TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "525d671d-3184-40ff-a92b-4cb3519061ad"],
 " the Gaussian fluctuations alone give ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["fl",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "/", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["Gi",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], "\[TildeTilde]", "3"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "637d4422-b185-4529-9965-ff9982f1bb44"],
 ". The width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Gi",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["c",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fd94c064-f747-482a-aa30-6d93e816358e"],
 " is larger than the critical temperature itself and of the order of the \
cutoff. The reason is in the table: the correlation length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Xi]", 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f0f76292-4a62-4649-9d77-22273c28984f"],
 " is about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalLambda]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bc36884d-0dcb-4308-b384-bc0c719df49b"],
 ", the shortest length of the model, because the pairs are tightly bound \
(there is no Fermi surface, and the pairing needs a coupling above the \
critical one), and the specific-heat jump per correlation volume is about \
0.04, far below 1: a correlation volume holds much less than one degree of \
freedom, while mean-field theory needs many. (In a superconductor of Bardeen, \
Cooper and Schrieffer the correlation length is large against the distance of \
the electrons and the Ginzburg number, of the order of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["c",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], "/", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["F",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}], "4"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46d8ac8a-8680-461b-a2b0-c8453233f767"],
 " with the Fermi energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["F",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79749601-b07e-413f-881d-29a93990ccc7"],
 ", is tiny; here the opposite holds.) The error of the regularization does \
not change the conclusion (the last column). ",
 StyleBox["What this means for Section III.T (a remark, and why it matters).",
  
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The statements of Section III.T.6 are statements about the mean-field free \
energy, and as such they are correct and checked. But the temperatures at \
which that free energy shows the behaviour of Landau's theory, from about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0.4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "90e607a2-b68c-4021-aa55-c66db2602115"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0.98", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "127091be-9c66-40ed-85d6-dba2e6b68771"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["c",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d7b6b9-7715-4f29-8fbb-227949eb6c92"],
 ", lie inside the critical region. The mean-field theory of the five methods \
therefore does not describe the superfluid near its transition: the critical \
temperatures, the exponent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b3b9eaf6-c79b-4c1f-a8ef-59d58c6ce4f3"],
 " of the order parameter and the continuity of the transition are not \
reliable. It matters because the five methods agree with each other there, \
and agreement among mean-field methods is no evidence when all of them omit \
the same fluctuations. A reliable description of the transition needs a \
calculation beyond the methods: for example the three-dimensional theory of a \
complex isospin vector with two quartic invariants and with the gauge fields \
on a lattice (the method used for the thermal transition of the electroweak \
theory by K. Kajantie, M. Laine, K. Rummukainen and M. Shaposhnikov, 1996), \
or the Gaussian fluctuations of the auxiliary pair field in HS (the method of \
P. Nozieres and S. Schmitt-Rink, 1985, for pairs bound more tightly than \
their distance)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cf42bb89-2151-4a50-9d86-69d125846e39"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
III.G.8 Can the superfluid play the role of the Higgs particle, and is the \
Higgs a composite particle?\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"37f2e3d1-2a8a-4554-b7dc-ba41070b8f4e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The Standard Model",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (the conventions of Section I.1): ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["gv", "TI"], "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d833b933-b83f-46c6-9105-c8043997d28b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["g", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"\[Prime]", "2"}]]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8a781992-68e2-417b-9e0f-db641e04c1c3"],
 ", the vacuum value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SqrtBox["2"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["F", "TI"]]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "2"}]], "\[LongEqual]", "246.22"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "82ef5cb9-62e7-4f59-a15f-d7a277dd2586"],
 " GeV with the Fermi constant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["F", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ae5e1f56-0ca8-4798-bb5d-e2e9b00ef30f"],
 ", the Higgs boson of the mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "125.20", "\[PlusMinus]", "0.11"}],
    TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a225e8b5-d388-4230-9ad1-877e52960ab2"],
 " GeV and the width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["3.7", 
     RowBox[{"-", "1.4"}], 
     RowBox[{"+", "1.9"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "470b49bd-a156-4ce3-81cf-a3ccbd920faa"],
 " MeV, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "80.3692", "\[PlusMinus]", 
    "0.0133"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6dd6c1-88c3-45b2-aca4-c3342d01e47f"],
 " GeV, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "91.1880", "\[PlusMinus]", 
    "0.0020"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "768b5190-830d-49ba-bbd8-2e9b821cfc13"],
 " GeV (Particle Data Group, S. Navas et al. 2024), and the quartic coupling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
     StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", "0.1293"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e0fbb560-2ced-4a7d-9e5f-3b571297ae7f"],
 ". ",
 StyleBox["The scale of the breaking.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["I",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f1840ac8-295c-4757-8405-636f7afdec98"],
 " with the isospin decay constant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["I",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c3370be2-1cae-4c8e-9d87-b67c1015ce39"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2837f86e-04d5-4485-9a72-307776fafb34"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "866f2179-f35c-4df6-b017-1086be3f6394"],
 " are the coefficients of the two invariants of the kinetic part of the \
field, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "+", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Dagger]"], "\[CenterDot]",
        "\[PartialD]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "/", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8567bef5-893f-4fdf-afb7-857ae32dfcb5"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70840521-7d20-4c19-93c7-e2cdae633df2"],
 " is the field of the vacuum at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fa333d17-cdb6-49a4-a886-d28c5a1a5e98"],
 "; the decay constant of the phase is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["SF",
           FontSlant->"Plain"], 
          StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["SF",
           FontSlant->"Plain"], 
          StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "87809ef8-0229-49c8-8d2a-9311ffc7738d"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "464b4759-1857-470b-9df6-83a961951b05"],
 ". The analogue of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["v", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8c19e116-3389-4664-b17b-1bdb527c080b"],
 " is therefore"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8954b70c-55cd-4e9e-b1ec-1572849793d6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "2", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["I",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ",", "      ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["v",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ",", "      ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ")"}], "2"]}]], ","}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"dcab45d8-3dd9-4215-8b35-78124fcaf1d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with the mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3803efe4-9edb-45e0-8d7e-e760af90908f"],
 " of the amplitude (Higgs) mode and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["NU",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d26c761a-f572-4034-a5db-632f352ccaed"],
 " of the non-unitary doublet from the linear response of Part II (the exact \
small oscillations of each method). ",
 StyleBox["The width of the amplitude mode.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " On the field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
       StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
      StyleBox["h", "TI"], "/", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           SubsuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["SF",
             FontSlant->"Plain"], 
            StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
           SubsuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["SF",
             FontSlant->"Plain"], 
            StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]]}], ")"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"]}]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "3"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e5d9c51e-ebf1-4df0-a4cf-ddbf24971ad2"],
 " (the amplitude field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f1f4f223-4055-4b78-9107-e16d28d2904b"],
 " normalized canonically and the phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "291bf52e-aed2-4983-9173-864216d4d48a"],
 "), and on the same field rotated about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "1"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aef1e7e1-01c0-4602-9e83-35169b3197e5"],
 " by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "1"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a9c6a892-4dae-4ab7-990c-135a586628b2"],
 ", the kinetic part contains the couplings ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"]}], ")"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]],
   "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d5551759-d8a7-48e3-832a-b1aa4e1df763"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
          StyleBox["I",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], "/", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["F",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], ")"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "1"]}], ")"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]],
   "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bd64fc0-192f-4f5d-854a-537775733092"],
 " (and the same for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5010333c-31f3-4dd7-82fb-79fb8205ed2b"],
 "). With the canonical Goldstone fields ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], 
    SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", "0"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e5f62096-13f2-4087-ad59-95d1e11e5133"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["I",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], 
    SubscriptBox["\[CurlyTheta]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "81a3def7-3fa5-449a-8110-40c701da681c"],
 " all three couplings are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c2dde21-f647-4fcb-943a-a5900c241f9d"],
 "; the decay of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5536ea00-3fcf-4427-9800-576f5987c65a"],
 " at rest into two massless quanta of one canonical field has the amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], "/", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["F",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d0bca80b-41b0-4889-97eb-da6461f40bef"],
 " and the width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "3"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"32", "\[Pi]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
          StyleBox["F",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "927b9e9b-7300-498b-9c77-b1d7c133ddc2"],
 " (the phase space of two identical massless particles), and the three \
channels give"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c2df5c4a-f167-4dcf-994b-a07065c5daa2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"3", "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
         StyleBox["H",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "3"]}], 
    RowBox[{"32", "\[Pi]", "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
         StyleBox["F",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"]}]], "."}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->1.25 
  Inherited,ExpressionUUID->"c0ad4a7b-e7ce-4439-9f2c-85f54f3c137f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With the gauge fields the Goldstone fields are the longitudinal parts of \
the massive gauge bosons (the equivalence theorem of J. M. Cornwall, D. N. \
Levin and G. Tiktopoulos 1974 and of M. S. Chanowitz and M. K. Gaillard \
1985), whose masses are at most about a fifth of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["H",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "410106d8-c3a1-4e47-9006-111b899975f3"],
 " (the phase-space factor is above 0.97). For the Standard Model with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["f", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dcab8c0a-7ddb-4ecb-97ec-b1b9eab75dd0"],
 " the same formula is the known width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "3"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"32", "\[Pi]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cc19a5dd-2b7c-4357-a4e1-cb30b6f93665"],
 " of a heavy Higgs boson. ",
 StyleBox["A remark on the width (what it means and why it matters).",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The formula uses the effective Lagrangian at the energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["H",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52402a04-1430-4cc5-99ec-ba1610991240"],
 ", where it is not accurate (its mass of the amplitude mode differs from the \
linear response by 7 to 17 per cent), so it estimates the order of magnitude \
only. It matters because the conclusion drawn from it, that the amplitude \
mode is a broad resonance and not a narrow particle, needs only the order of \
magnitude: the width is 2 to 4 times the mass. The next cell derives the two \
couplings by exact differentiation of the kinetic part (symbolic, with real \
symbols), and compares them with the closed forms and the Rust values."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d3290f3-dd04-4933-9a01-78701f0f881a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
    "the", " ", "couplings", " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", "amplitude", " ", 
     "field", " ", "to", " ", "the", " ", "Goldstone", " ", "fields", " ", 
     "by", " ", "exact", " ", "differentiation", " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", 
     "kinetic", " ", "part", " ", "along", " ", "a", " ", "line", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"gzX", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"the", " ", "field", " ", "at", " ", "gzX", " ", "is", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"gzP0", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gzAmp", "/", "gzNh"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"e", "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"i", " ", "gzD0", " ", "gzX"}], ")"}]}], " ", "R_", "1", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "gzX"}], ")"}], " ", "e_", "3", " ", "with", " ",
        "the", " ", "constant", " ", "amplitude", " ", "gzAmp", " ", "and", " ",
        "the", "\n", "   ", "gradients", " ", "gzD0"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gzD1", " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", "two", " ", "angles", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"R_", "1"}], ":", " ", 
        RowBox[{"the", " ", "rotation", " ", "about", " ", "e_", "1"}]}], 
       ")"}]}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gzKin", " ", "is", " ", "Z"}], " ", "|", "dPhi", "|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", "Y"}], " ", "|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Phi", "^", "dag"}], " ", "dPhi"}], "|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"^", "2"}], "/"}], "|", "Phi", "|", 
       RowBox[{
